==Trivia==
* The number of Pokémon {{Adv|Green}} found includes her Snubbull and Lugia.
* No chapters from this volume are included in the compilation volume [[The Best of Pokémon Adventures: Yellow]].
* This was the last volume to be published in {{pmin|France}} by Glénat.
* The Message from [[Mato]] featured in this volume mentions there being a hint regarding what the future has in store for the manga after the release of {{game|Gold and Silver|s}} hidden in the book. There are actually several:
** In ''[[PS072|Weezing Winks Out]]'', [[Koga]] passes [[Paralyze Heal|Parlyz Heal]] to {{adv|Blue}} by sending him a [[Poké Ball]] with a Pokémon [[held item|holding]] it, a mechanic introduced in [[Generation II]].
** In ''[[PS078|Victim of Venusaur]]'', {{adv|Red}} orders [[Saur]] to use {{m|Sweet Scent}}, a move introduced in [[Generation II]].
** The Pokédex analysis at the end of the book lists {{adv|Green}} as having seen 153 Pokémon species, despite [[Generation I]] featuring only 151.

===Errors===
====VIZ Media second edition====
* On page 45, [[PS068#Errors|there is a blank word balloon]].
* On page 142, {{type|Ground}} is called the "Earth-type".

===Translation edits===
====VIZ Media second edition====
* The last two pages of the volume containing analyses of {{adv|Yellow}}'s, {{adv|Green}}'s and {{adv|Blue}}'s [[Pokédex]] are omitted.
* In all of its appearances throughout the book, {{p|Jynx}}'s skin color is changed from black to gray in order to match its purple redesign following the [[Pokémon controversies#Jynx|Jynx controversy]].


